{"id": "EUVD-2026-5842", "enisaUuid": "bd20ead0-1d13-3267-b558-d235a225ad72", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nspi: tegra210-quad: Protect curr_xfer in tegra_qspi_combined_seq_xfer\n\nThe curr_xfer field is read by the IRQ handler without holding the lock\nto check if a transfer is in progress. When clearing curr_xfer in the\ncombined sequence transfer loop, protect it with the spinlock to prevent\na race with the interrupt handler.\n\nProtect the curr_xfer clearing at the exit path of\ntegra_qspi_combined_seq_xfer() with the spinlock to prevent a race\nwith the interrupt handler that reads this field.\n\nWithout this protection, the IRQ handler could read a partially updated\ncurr_xfer value, leading to NULL pointer dereference or use-after-free.", "datePublished": "2026-02-14T16:27:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T18:35:38", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9fa4262a80f751d14a6a39d2c03f57db68da2618", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/762e2ce71c8f0238e9eaf05d14da803d9a24422f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/712cde8d916889e282727cdf304a43683adf899e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6fd446178a610a48e80e5c5b487b0707cd01daac", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3bc293d5b56502068481478842f57b3d96e432c7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bf4528ab28e2bf112c3a2cdef44fd13f007781cd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-23202", "GHSA-g2fg-h3fh-wpj6"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.1, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "11442ff7-5ec7-3578-bc6e-6ae6f598f4e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "83309dd551cfd60a5a1a98d9cab19f435b44d46d <762e2ce71c8f0238e9eaf05d14da803d9a24422f"}, {"id": "25ecf3dd-6ac8-35cd-84f1-abe26a68db70", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb0c58be84f907285af45657c1d4847b960a12bf"}, {"id": "34ac1bdc-1174-3dd7-96df-7195996bab43", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b4e